  "reasoning": "Key discovery during drafting: the design doc's section 3.1 triple table (.claude/specs/callisto-matrix.md) is NOT byte-identical to the actual triple_to_role match arms in crates/callisto-graph/src/napi.rs today. The doc lists wasm32-wasi and armv7-unknown-linux-musleabihf; the code recognises wasm32-wasip1 and wasm32-unknown-unknown instead, and has no musleabihf arm variant. Since REQ-007 explicitly mandates reusing triple_to_role and NOT duplicating the table, I anchored the spec's authoritative triple list on the actual code (verified by reading napi.rs directly) rather than the stale doc prose, and called this out explicitly in scope and AC-012 so the implementer builds the hostRunner/useCross/artifactName table against the real 18 triples, not the doc's list. Also discovered: triple_to_role's ManifestRole::Platform only carries platform/arch/abi -- it has no concept of hostRunner/useCross/artifactName, so that mapping is unavoidably NEW code in matrix.rs, keyed by triple, not an extension of napi.rs (consistent with the non-goal 'no modification to napi.rs'). Also discovered: callisto-manifests has no existing reader for [tool.maturin].targets or engines.node — python.rs only parses requires-python for a different purpose (Poetry 2.x project table) — so both are new manifest-reading code, called out in scope. Placed MatrixReport/PlatformTargetGroup/PlatformTarget/RuntimeVersionEntry in callisto-model (following the StatusReport precedent) but noted graph-layer placement is an acceptable alternative since this is an implementation/module-boundary decision, not a contract decision — the JSON shape and field names are what's load-bearing for AC purposes, not the crate they live in. Kept the composite-action (section 7 of design doc) optional per REQ-007's explicit 'nice-to-have if time allows' language, but made the action.yml wiring change (section 6.1 jq pipeline) a hard AC since REQ-007 lists it as a done_when item, not a nice-to-have.\n\nFixes applied from canon-auditor round 1: (1) matrix()'s signature corrected from a non-compiling `Result<MatrixReport, CliError>` (callisto-graph cannot name CliError -- wrong dependency direction) and a bare `&Workspace` (missing required lifetime/generics) to match the real status()/plan_publish() pattern: `pub fn matrix<R: CommandRunner, D: DependencyResolver>(ws: &Workspace<'_, R, D>, opts: &MatrixOptions) -> Result<MatrixReport, GraphError>`, verified against crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/status.rs:59-62. (2) Added AC-010b covering malformed package.json (JSON) parse failure, mirroring AC-010's TOML case -- the original spec only covered the TOML side of a dual-format read pass. (3) Added AC-017 specifying that a package declaring both napi.targets and [tool.maturin].targets is a hard GraphError, not undefined behavior -- api_surface updated to name the new GraphError::ConflictingPlatformTargetSources variant. (4) Fixed the previously-unpinned 'DiagnosticCode::UnrecognisedPlatformTriple or equivalent' to an exact variant name with a pinned kebab-case serde string, added AC-018 asserting the serialization round-trip and requiring a docs/01-spec.md G.13 table row, matching the established convention SPEC-002 set for BareRuleMatchesMultipleEcosystems. (5) AC-016 tightened from an ambiguous 'or an equivalent shell pipeline' to a precise byte-for-byte (whitespace-insensitive) jq-filter-text requirement, leaving only the shell wrapper's cosmetic details unconstrained. (6) Scope clarified: crates/callisto-graph/src/matrix.rs holds private read/assembly logic; crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/matrix.rs holds the public entry point -- both files exist, matching the commands/publish.rs -> apply.rs/groups.rs precedent, resolving the prior ambiguity about whether one or two files were intended.\n\nFixes applied from canon-auditor round 2: (1) AC-017's GraphError::ConflictingPlatformTargetSources was underspecified ('..' field list, no code/help text) -- pinned to an exact field list (package, napi_source, maturin_source), diagnostic code E118 (next available after E117 UnexpectedManifestVersion), and #[error(...)]/#[diagnostic(help(...))] text matching the shape of every other recent GraphError variant in crates/callisto-graph/src/error.rs. (2) Added AC-010c covering schema-valid-but-wrong-type manifest fields (napi.targets present as a non-array, [tool.maturin].targets present as a non-array, engines.node/requires-python present as a non-string) -- AC-010/AC-010b only covered syntax errors, not type/schema violations on an otherwise-parseable manifest. (3) Added AC-001b specifying that an explicitly-empty napi.targets = [] produces a present-but-empty platformTargets entry, distinguishable from the field being entirely absent (AC-003) -- previously undefined which of two valid interpretations applied. (4) AC-011's is_error_case corrected from true to false: it is a warning-only, exit-0 success path (the call succeeds, other targets still populate the report), unlike every other is_error_case:true criterion in this spec (AC-007, AC-010, AC-010b, AC-010c, AC-017), which all fail with a non-zero exit code -- the field now consistently means 'the CLI process exits non-zero' across all criteria that assert it true.\n\nFixes applied from canon-exit-gate round 3 (blocking): (1) --format json|table was unbuildable: crates/callisto-cli/src/cli.rs GlobalArgs.format is global=true over OutputFormat::{Text,Json} (no Table variant, default_value=\"text\"), and a global clap arg cannot be shadowed by a same-named subcommand arg. Resolved by dropping the subcommand-local --format entirely and reusing the global text|json flag exactly like every existing subcommand (verified pattern: crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/status.rs:41 `match global.format`) -- Text renders the table, Json renders MatrixReport. Added AC-003b pinning the bare-invocation (no flag) default to text/table, matching every other subcommand's no-flag behavior. AC-008 renamed from --format table to --format text. (2) AC-011's warning diagnostic had no field to live in: MatrixReport was pinned to exactly two fields and AC-003 pinned the full empty-output bytes, leaving no room for a diagnostic without contradicting AC-003. Resolved by adding schema_version and diagnostics fields to MatrixReport and implementing the Report trait, following the exact StatusReport precedent (crates/callisto-model/src/report.rs:297-317, diagnostics: Vec<Diagnostic> with #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \"Vec::is_empty\")]); AC-003 updated to the new exact empty-output bytes ({\"schemaVersion\":1,...}, no diagnostics key when empty); AC-011 updated to assert the diagnostic appears in diagnostics[] with DiagnosticCode::UnrecognisedPlatformTriple. (3) AC-012 let the hostRunner/useCross table be anything satisfying only 'non-empty string, boolean field' -- an implementation mapping every triple to ubuntu-latest/false would have passed all 21 criteria while producing a matrix that builds no darwin or windows artifact. Resolved by pinning the exact (hostRunner, useCross) pair for all 18 real triples, derived from the design doc's per-platform-family table (.claude/specs/callisto-matrix.md section 3.1) corrected for the two triple-name discrepancies already established (wasm32-wasip1 not wasm32-wasi; no musleabihf arm) and extended to cover wasm32-unknown-unknown (absent from the doc's table entirely; assigned ubuntu-latest/false to match its sibling wasm32-wasip1 entry, since neither wasm target requires cross-compilation tooling). (4) AC-015's is_error_case corrected from true to false: it is a compile-time/type-level deserialization assertion inside a unit test with no CLI process or exit code involved, which does not fit the round-2-established definition of is_error_case (the CLI process exits non-zero) that every other true-marked criterion (AC-007, AC-010, AC-010b, AC-010c, AC-017) satisfies.\n\nFixes applied from canon-exit-gate round 4 (blocking, both